<title>BELGIUM: EU takes Austria to Court over Brenner road tolls.</title>
<headline>EU takes Austria to Court over Brenner road tolls.</headline>
<text>
<p>BRUSSELS, July 30 - The European Commission said on Wednesday it would refer the case of toll increases on Austria's Brenner motorway to the European Court of Justice.</p>
<p>The EU executive said it believed the toll increases were discriminatory and not related to the costs of building and operating the motorway as is required by EU law.</p>
<p>Austria has justified higher toll rates on the grounds of cost increases for the entire Austrian motorway network and as a way of diverting smaller domestic traffic onto secondary roads.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission sympathises with Austria's concern to protect the environment,&quot; EU transport commissioner Neil Kinnock said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;But this unilateral and discriminatory action is...not only an infringement of EU law...but cannot provide long-term environmental safeguards.&quot;</p>
